DBMS Viva + Practical Master Notes (SPPU SE 2024 Pattern)
1. What is DBMS?
DBMS (Database Management System) is software used to create, store, manage and retrieve data efficiently.
2. What is Database?
A database is an organized collection of related data stored electronically.
3. What is Table?
A table is a collection of rows and columns used to store data.
4. What is Tuple?
A tuple is a single row or record in a table.
5. What is Attribute?
An attribute is a column in a table.
6. What is SQL?
SQL is Structured Query Language used to manage databases.
7. What is DDL?
DDL defines database structure. Commands: CREATE, ALTER, DROP.
8. What is DML?
DML modifies data. Commands: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE.
9. What is DCL?
DCL controls permissions. Commands: GRANT, REVOKE.
10. What is TCL?
TCL manages transactions. Commands: COMMIT, ROLLBACK.
11. CRUD Operations
Create, Read, Update, Delete.
12. Primary Key
Uniquely identifies each record in a table.
13. Foreign Key
Connects two tables using primary key reference.
14. Super Key
Uniquely identifies records.
15. Candidate Key
Minimal super key.
16. Alternate Key
Candidate key not selected as primary key.
17. What is JOIN?
Combines rows from multiple tables.
18. INNER JOIN
Returns matching rows from both tables.
19. LEFT JOIN
Returns all rows from left table and matching rows from right table.
20. RIGHT JOIN
Returns all rows from right table and matching rows from left table.
21. FULL JOIN
Returns all rows from both tables.
22. Normalization
Organizing data to reduce redundancy.
23. 1NF
All attributes contain atomic values.
24. 2NF
No partial dependency.
25. 3NF
No transitive dependency.
26. View
A virtual table created from SQL query.
27. Transaction
Sequence of operations treated as single unit.
28. ACID Properties
Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability.
29. Cursor
Processes rows one by one.
30. Types of Cursor
Implicit Cursor and Explicit Cursor.
31. Parameterized Cursor
Cursor accepting parameters.
32. Trigger
Automatically executes on INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE.
33. Types of Trigger
BEFORE Trigger and AFTER Trigger.
34. OLD vs NEW
OLD = previous value, NEW = updated value.
35. Stored Procedure
Precompiled SQL code stored in database.
36. Function
Stored program returning value.
37. Procedure vs Function
Procedure may not return value; function always returns value.
38. DELETE vs DROP
DELETE removes rows; DROP removes table.
39. Aggregation
Combines multiple values into one result.
40. Aggregation Functions
COUNT, SUM, AVG, MAX, MIN.
41. Indexing
Improves searching speed.
42. Aggregation vs Indexing
Aggregation summarizes data; indexing speeds searching.
43. insertOne vs insertMany
insertOne inserts single document; insertMany inserts multiple documents.
44. DBMS vs RDBMS
DBMS stores data generally; RDBMS stores relational tabular data.
45. File in DBMS
Collection of related records stored together.
Important Syntax Examples
Operation Syntax
Create Table CREATE TABLE student(id INT, name VARCHAR(20));
Insert INSERT INTO student VALUES(1,'Ved');
Select SELECT * FROM student;
Update UPDATE student SET marks=90 WHERE id=1;
Delete DELETE FROM student WHERE id=1;
Drop DROP TABLE student;
Create Index CREATE INDEX idx_name ON students(name);
MongoDB insertOne db.users.insertOne({name:'Ved'})
MongoDB insertMany db.users.insertMany([{name:'Ved'}])
MongoDB find db.users.find()
